# Preventive, not a fix for a current bug: build.sh is committed with LF today
# (core.autocrlf=true normalises on commit). This pins that guarantee.
#
# Why it matters: the repo is developed on Windows and deployed to Linux. If a .sh
# file ever reaches the repo with CRLF, the trailing \r becomes part of the shebang
# and Linux reports:
#
#     /usr/bin/env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory
#
# which reads like a missing interpreter rather than a line-ending problem.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Windows-only, wants CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Never apply text conversion to the DuckDB warehouse or other binaries.
*.duckdb binary
*.duckdb.wal binary
*.parquet binary
